      "content": "the regs only matter if people actually know what's inside the code. most people just click \"accept\" on the terms and conditions without a clue. it makes me wonder if there's a way to actually check for this kind of thing. like, if there was a covert data-harvesting program like this, what kind of technical red flags should i be looking for in my own device? is there any way to tell if the shoe is sending more than just step counts to their servers?",
